   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Kylie,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve been running into an error for low-<i>m/z</i> datasets: &quot;Error in getMatrix(x) : negative extents to matrix&quot;. I have been using a Sciex 5800 (Analyze 7.5 data) looking at the range <i>m/z</i> 150-1500, so I&#39;m not sure where the &quot;negative&quot; is coming in. Using all of the same code (just changing file names), I haven&#39;t had this problem with higher <i>m/z</i> range datasets (900-4000). Any help would be greatly appreciated,</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Andrew Goodenough</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "MxgHeCsyAwAJ",
   "from": "Melanie Föll",
   "author": "db2a70d9b31cb1f7",
   "date": "2018-10-12T10:34:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: Analyze 7.5 Read Error: Negative Extents to Matrix",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Kylie, <br></div><div><br></div><div>I get the same error in v1.12 and v1.12.1 with all Analyze7.5 files except for one test file with 9 pixels and a m/z range of 150. All the Analyze7.5 files come from the same MS and have worked with the previous Cardinalversions but in v.1.12 I get the same error as Andrew.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Any help would be appreciated. <br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Melanie<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ZxXepvlHAwAJ",
